> Not really - remember that "hit points" is just an abstration of the
> character's physical endurance. The reason a grid bug's bite takes off
> 1/10th of your HP at level 1 is because the character is only able to
> endure ten bites. A level 2 character, meanwhile, can endure twice as
> much, and as such their max HP is 20 rather than 10.
>
> However, a half disintegration attack isn't a normal kind of attack. It
> is functionally different from the standard sword slice which one's
> tempered flesh or iron resolve can resist. If it hits, it causes a
> portion of the character's body mass to crumble away into nothing,
> without fail. As such, there is no character that can endure two
> consecutive hits of it. So, it does the same percentage of damage to
> all of them.

The problem is, in some sense, that I usually don't feel the need to heal  
when I'm at 195/400 while I might do feel it a bit more at 55/100.  
Half-disintegration resistance changes that. Maybe a better way would be  
for half-disintegration to make you loss a fixed amount of HP and a  
certain amount of max HP. It still better than being wiped into tiny  
particles at once...

However, as I've mentionned, (half)-disintegration resistance is almost  
pointless since the two source of disintegration can be protected either  
by reflection that you want anyway or by not angering your god (I think I  
cannot remember when was the last time  angered my god)

