Indeed, spliting MR into MR (protect from magical damage) ans SR (protect  
 from magical non-damage effects) makes sense. However, magical damages are  
not that anoying in the end (reflection protects from some of them and the  
rest is "mere" damage while non-damage effect may be much more nasty). So  
everybody is going to want SR and not MR ("half spell damage" artefacts  
are not on everybody AK). Making SR hard to get actually reduce the AK  
choice at this point. Maybe GD should indeed live in the realm of SR  
rather than MR and MR be closer to the current half spell damage. It's  
good but not vital. Add a few mundane (not artefacts) objects providing it  
but I think that restricting the number of objects providing SR (compared  
to the curretn MR providers) is not that good. I, for one, will go for SR  
at any price and then look after MR. If only a cloak provides SR then, it  
will be cloak of SR asap.

I would say keep SR for the GD(SM) maybe make half-SR give 90% chance of  
resisting the effect (you can avoid a chance encounter with it but not  
rely on it in the long run). Give SR to all (or most of) current  
MR-providing artefacts. Maybe even add another SR provider (an helmet ?  
(because magic acts on mind and for a change...)) On the other side, maybe  
turn all half-spell damage artefacts into MR (or at least half MR which is  
almost the same thing), maybe add a MR-providing dragon. Add a  
MR-providing amulet or ring.



